  Provenance: Depth is a declared convention, not a measurement. The object is an irregular cloud with no symmetry to deproject, so each point is placed about a surface undulating with a low-frequency noise field, spread wider where the plate is brighter. Only the colour and the two-dimensional structure come from the photograph.
